{"G1306":{"id":"G1306","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1306","disambiguated_id":"G1306 = a Combination of","unique_id":"G0826 (G1223+G0826)","headword":"διαυγάζω","transliteration":"diaugazō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to shine through","definition_en":"δι-αυγάζω \n [in Aq.: Job.25:5 * ;] \nto shine through, to dawn: 2Pe.1:19 (cf. ἕως οὗ διαπνεύσῃ ἡ ἡμέρα, Gal.2:17).†\n (AS)","source_line":1438}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"clareie","count":1}]},"G1893":{"id":"G1893","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1893","disambiguated_id":"G1893 =","unique_id":"G1893","headword":"ἐπεί","transliteration":"epei","lexical_morphology":"G:CONJ","gloss_en":"since","definition_en":"ἐπεί \n conj. (ἐπί, εἰ), \n when, since; \n __1. of time, when, after: Luk.7:1 (Rec., WH, mg.). \n __2. Of cause, since, because: Mat.18:32 21:46 27:6, Mrk.15:42, Luk.1:34, Jhn.13:29 19:31, Act.13:46 (Rec., WH, mg.), 1Co.14:12, 2Co.11:18 13:3, Heb.5:2, 11 6:13 9:17 11:11; ἐ. οὖν, Heb.2:14 4:6. With ellipsis, otherwise, else: Rom.11:6, 22, Heb.9:26; ἐ. ἄρα, 1Co.5:10 7:14; introducing a question, Rom.3:6, 1Co.14:16 15:29, Heb.10:2 (cf. 4Ma.1:33 4Mac 2:7 4Mac 2:10 4Mac 4:24-26).†\n (AS)","source_line":2034}],"occurrence_count":26,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"porque","count":8},{"gloss":"pois","count":8},{"gloss":"outra","count":4},{"gloss":"vez","count":2},{"gloss":"modo","count":1},{"gloss":"visto-que","count":1},{"gloss":"doutra-maneira","count":1},{"gloss":"contrário","count":1}]},"G2083":{"id":"G2083","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2083","disambiguated_id":"G2083 =","unique_id":"G2083","headword":"ἑταῖρος","transliteration":"hetairos","lexical_morphology":"G:N-M","gloss_en":"friend","definition_en":"ἑταῖρος, -ου, ὁ \n [in LXX chiefly for רֵעַ and cognate forms, also Sir.11:6 37:2 ff., al. ;] \na companion, comrade: Mat.11:16 (WH, ἑτέροις); voc., as term of address, my friend: Mat.20:13 22:12 26:50.†\n (AS)","source_line":2225}],"occurrence_count":3,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"amigo","count":3}]},"G2106":{"id":"G2106","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2106","disambiguated_id":"G2106 =","unique_id":"G2106","headword":"εὐδοκέω","transliteration":"eudokeō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to delight","definition_en":"εὐ-δοκέω, -ῶ\n (on the derivation, see EL, § 28, 6) [in LXX chiefly for רָצָה, also for אָבָה, חָפֵץ, etc. ;] \n__1. with inf. (Polyb., al.), to be well pleased, to think it good, to give consent (so frequently in π. in legal docu­ments; Milligan, Th., 22 f.): Luk.12:32, Rom.15:26-27, 1Co.1:21, Gal.1:15, Col.1:19, R, mg. (ICC, in l, but see infr.), 1Th.2:8 3:1; μᾶλλον εὐ., 2Co.5:8; with accusative and inf. (Polyb., i, 8, 4), Col, l.with, R, txt. (Lft., in l). \n __2. to be well pleased or take pleasure with or in a person or thing; \n __(a) with dative (Polyb., al.; 1Ma.1:43, I Est.4:39): 2Th.2:12; \n __(b) as frequently in LXX, \n __α with accusative: Mat.12:13, Heb.10:5, 8\" (LXX) ; \n __β before ἐν (cf. Heb. בּ רָצָה, Psa.149:4): Mat.3:17 17:5, Mrk.1:11, Luk.3:22 (on the tense, see M, Pr., 134 f.; DCG, i,308 b), 1Co.10:5, 2Co.12:10, Heb.10:38\" (LXX) ; \n __(with) before εἰς: 2Pe.1:17. (cf. συν-ευδοκέω, and see Cremer, 213 f.; Field, Notes, 48 f.; DCG, i, 355a.)†\n (AS)","source_line":2248}],"occurrence_count":21,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"agrado","count":7},{"gloss":"agradou","count":3},{"gloss":"prazer","count":2},{"gloss":"agradaram","count":2},{"gloss":"minha","count":1},{"gloss":"pareceu","count":1},{"gloss":"queremos","count":1},{"gloss":"me-comprazo","count":1},{"gloss":"aquele","count":1},{"gloss":"queríamos","count":1},{"gloss":"decidimos","count":1}]},"G2123":{"id":"G2123","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2123","disambiguated_id":"G2123 =","unique_id":"G2123","headword":"εὐκοπώτερος","transliteration":"eukopōteros","lexical_morphology":"G:A","gloss_en":"easy","definition_en":"εὔ-κοπος, -ον \n [in LXX: Sir.22:15, 1Ma.3:18 * ;] \nwith easy labour, easy: compar., -ώτερόν ἐστι, with inf., Mat.9:5, Mrk.2:9, Luk.5:23; with accusative and inf., Mat.19:24, Mrk.10:25, Luk.16:17 18:25 (Polyb.; the adv. -ως occurs in Aristoph., Fr., 615).†\n (AS)","source_line":2265}],"occurrence_count":7,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"fácil","count":7}]},"G2199":{"id":"G2199","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2199","disambiguated_id":"G2199G =","unique_id":"G2199G","headword":"Ζεβεδαῖος","transliteration":"Zebedaios","lexical_morphology":"N:N-M-P","gloss_en":"Zebedee","definition_en":"Ζεβεδαῖος, -ου, ὁ (Heb. זְבַדְיָה; LXX: Ζαβδειά, Est.8:8 10:20; Ζαβαδαῖας, I Est.9:35; Ζαβαδαῖος, I Est.9:21) \n Zebedee, father of James and John the Apostles: Mat.4:21 10:2 20:20 26:37 27:56, Mrk.1:19-20 3:17 10:35, Luk.5:10, Jhn.21:2.†\n (AS)","source_line":2342}],"occurrence_count":12,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"Zebedeu","count":12}]},"G245":{"id":"G245","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G0245","disambiguated_id":"G0245 =","unique_id":"G0245","headword":"ἀλλότριος","transliteration":"allotrios","lexical_morphology":"G:A","gloss_en":"another’s","definition_en":"ἀλλότριος, -α, -ον\n (ἄλλος), [in LXX for זוּר, נֵכָר, אַחֵר ;] \n__1. be-longing to another, not one's own (opposite to ἴδιος): Luk.16:12, Rom.14:4 15:20 (Field, Notes, 165 f.), 2Co.10:15-16, 1Ti.5:22, Heb.9:25. \n __2. foreign, strange, alien (opposite to οἰκεῖος; see MM, VGT, see word): Mat.17:25-26, Jhn.10:5, Act.7:6, Heb.11:9, 34.†\n (AS)","source_line":347}],"occurrence_count":14,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"outros","count":5},{"gloss":"alheio","count":2},{"gloss":"estranho","count":1},{"gloss":"estranhos","count":1},{"gloss":"alheia","count":1},{"gloss":"construísse","count":1},{"gloss":"alheios-conserva","count":1},{"gloss":"terra","count":1},{"gloss":"exércitos","count":1}]},"G2801":{"id":"G2801","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2801","disambiguated_id":"G2801 =","unique_id":"G2801","h